  "claim": "An ESA astronaut was in command of an event. He has been to space more times than Frank De Winne. Soyuz TMA-08M was part of this event.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Hans Schlegel. Sentence: Hans Wilhelm Schlegel (Überlingen, 3 August 1951) is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: Frank, Viscount De Winne (born 25 April 1961, in Ledeberg, Belgium) is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He is Belgium's second person in space (after Dirk Frimout).\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\nPage: Expedition 35. Sentence: Expedition 35 was also only the second time an ISS crew is led by neither a NASA astronaut, nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009, when ESA astronaut Frank De Winne was in command.\nPage: Soyuz TMA-08M. Sentence: It transported three members of the Expedition 35 crew to the International Space Station.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Hans Schlegel. Sentence: Hans Wilhelm Schlegel (Überlingen, 3 August 1951) is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: Frank, Viscount De Winne (born 25 April 1961, in Ledeberg, Belgium) is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He is Belgium's second person in space (after Dirk Frimout).\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\nPage: Expedition 35. Sentence: Expedition 35 was also only the second time an ISS crew is led by neither a NASA astronaut, nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009, when ESA astronaut Frank De Winne was in command.\nPage: Soyuz TMA-08M. Sentence: It transported three members of the Expedition 35 crew to the International Space Station.",
